namespace pdg {
/**
\struct ColliderContact
\ingroup Physics Events
\brief One shape contact delivered as eventType_ColliderContact.

Enable Collider::setWantsContactEvents() on each collider whose owner should
receive notifications. Both Sprite and Part colliders deliver through the owning
Sprite. Each receiving collider sees itself as `collider`; vectors reverse for
the other endpoint. Delivery occurs synchronously after the solve.

\htmlonly[block]
<div class="shared-api-options">
\endhtmlonly

\anchor collider_contact_fields
\par Contact fields

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| emitter | Owning Sprite receiving this event |
| eventType | pdg::eventType_ColliderContact |
| collider, other | Shared Collider handles identifying both endpoints |
| shape, otherShape | Stable shape IDs within the corresponding colliders |
| phase | collision_Begin, collision_Stay or collision_End |
| point | Approximate contact Point in owning-layer/world coordinates |
| normal | Unit Vector directed from collider toward other |
| impulse | Actual impulse applied to other; zero for sensors, sleeping contacts and end contacts |
| penetration | Nonnegative overlap depth; zero for an end contact |
| sensor | Whether either collider is a sensor |

\htmlonly[block]
</div>
\endhtmlonly

Chipmunk contacts reuse its solved manifold: point is the mean of the contact
midpoints and penetration is the greatest overlap depth. Sleeping pairs continue
to report collision_Stay without a new impulse.

Geometry, filters and physical associations are evaluated for the solved frame.
A callback can remove an endpoint before another notification is delivered;
retained handles remain safe and isAttached() reports their current state.
Contact identity is per shape pair, so compound geometry can generate several
notifications for the same two owners. Native ColliderContact pointers are
borrowed only for the callback; JavaScript retains its Collider handles.
*/
/**
\var eventType_ColliderContact
\ingroup Events
\brief Collider begin/stay/end notification carrying a ColliderContact payload.
\see Collider::setWantsContactEvents()
*/
}
